      "writtenOn": "2026-03-06T17:05:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we need to submit an empty command buffer here? Or should we just register an OutstandingSubmission that will invoke the finish procs?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 52,
        "endLine": 15,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "3e68b4c0ac642c9ad375f622f66a4482a8e1b658",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "98fd5011_76bce0b3",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 19434
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-06T17:21:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But currently only `onSubmitToGPU` can return an OutstandingSubmission. Chrome uses an empty recording just to know when all previously submitted command buffer complete. Do you suggest we should add a new implementation of `OutstandingSubmission` that just checks the last submitted command buffer\u0027s status?\n\nI think submitting an empty command buffer is no harm currently (it is already happening). Maybe I can create a TODO?",
      "parentUuid": "f96d288b_a7411650",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 52,
        "endLine": 15,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "3e68b4c0ac642c9ad375f622f66a4482a8e1b658",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a906e29e_c9aed23c",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-06T17:27:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, it would basically be a `FinishedGpuSubmission` or similar name that returns true from `onIsFinished()` and does nothing in `onWaitUntilFinished()`. That way, it is just a marker in the outstanding submissions queue and triggers the callbacks in the right spot in the timeline.\n\nUnderlying GPU command buffers aren\u0027t trivial objects so while we are currently getting away with it, it seems a bit wasteful.",
      "parentUuid": "98fd5011_76bce0b3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 52,
        "endLine": 15,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "3e68b4c0ac642c9ad375f622f66a4482a8e1b658",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "29820854_6202caeb",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 19434
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-10T12:29:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "if `onWaitUntilFinished()` did nothing, would the `submit(syncToCpu::kYes)` call work incorrectly? The wait would return immediately but the real GPU work wouldn\u0027t complete yet.",
      "parentUuid": "a906e29e_c9aed23c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 52,
        "endLine": 15,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "3e68b4c0ac642c9ad375f622f66a4482a8e1b658",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0dacc074_7c074b0e",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-10T13:25:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah good catch, I\u0027d been thinking that `submit(syncToCpu::kYes)` would wait oldest-to-newest so when we reached the newest `FinishedGpuSubmission` it could just return. But `checkForFinishedWork` is written to assume that the GPU\u0027s waiting APIs will trigger in order, so we can just block on the newest submission and then clean up the prior submissions too.\n\nIt does seem wasteful to call `waitUntilFinished()` on all of the outstanding work submissions if we were to restructure the `checkForFinishedWork` but there probably aren\u0027t that many at a time. This could look something like:\n```\ndo {\n    OutstandingSubmission* front \u003d (OutstandingSubmission*)fOutstandingSubmissions.front();\n    if (front \u0026\u0026 sync \u003d\u003d SyncToCpu::kYes) {\n        (*front)-\u003ewaitUntilFinished(fSharedContext);\n    }\n    // For SyncToCPU, isFinished() should return true but this catches\n    // spurious interrupts when waiting on a semaphore.\n    while (front \u0026\u0026 (*front)-\u003eisFinished(fSharedContext)) {\n        fOutstandingSubmissions.pop_front();\n\n        front-\u003e~OutstandingSubmission();\n        front \u003d (OutstandingSubmission*)fOutstandingSubmissions.front();\n    }\n} while (sync \u003d\u003d SyncToCpu::kYes \u0026\u0026 !fOutstandingSubmissions.empty());\n```\n\nAnother option that could work would be that if we have an empty recording insertion, we just append the finished procs to the back outstanding work submission, or run them ASAP if there is no outstanding work.",
      "parentUuid": "29820854_6202caeb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 52,
        "endLine": 15,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "3e68b4c0ac642c9ad375f622f66a4482a8e1b658",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "461da5f2_e92c85eb",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
